# A wiki page's route changing under its in-flight reads (web/src/wiki.tsx:
# useLoad, WikiPage, WikiPageView), and the editor and Save that read the
# page on screen.
#
# The world: two pages, A and B, and the rest of the wiki ("away": the
# index, Review, Activity; all three are one useLoad each and leave the
# page view unmounted). Moving between them is a link, the palette or
# Back/Forward: each is a new route, and the model does not tell them
# apart.
#
# The product as it is. useLoad's effect clears data and error when its
# key changes and starts a read; the read's .then calls setData/setErr
# with nothing checking the key is still the one it was started for, so
# every read ever started lands on whatever screen is up when it answers
# (`live` only stops the next poll). Page reads do not poll.
# WikiPageView's head is `at = page?.path ?? path`: the path of the data
# shown, else the route's. Its reset effect (editor, history) is keyed on
# `at`, so it fires when the shown page changes, not when the route does.
# Edit seeds the editor with the shown page's body; Save PUTs it to
# route.path as it was when Save was clicked, then reloads that path with
# the load of that render.
#
# The claims the flow was mapped with, which the product does not meet;
# each was added as an assertion and fizz found the counterexample:
#   DataMatchesRoute (route in ["A","B"] -> shown in ["", route]):
#     Init, OpenA, OpenB, AnswerA: A's page under route B.
#   EditorMatchesRoute (editing in ["", route]):
#     ... AnswerA, Edit: the editor on route B holds A's body.
#   PutWritesItsOwnPath (not wrongwrite):
#     ... Edit, Save, SaveOk: A's body PUT to B, committed as an edit of B.
#   LateReadChangesNothing (not late):
#     Init, OpenA, OpenB, AnswerA.
#   always eventually ShowsItsPage (route away, or shown == route, or an
#   error): fizz's cycle reopens A and B around a late AnswerA; the
#   plainest is Init, OpenA, OpenB, AnswerB, AnswerA, after which nothing
#   is in flight and route B shows A for good.
# And one the mapping did not name: an editor open on route B over a late
# A is closed, text and all, when B's own read lands (the head moves).
# The same unguarded useLoad backs the index, Review, Activity and the
# source pane; they are outside this flow.
#
# Fields:
#   route      "away" | "A" | "B": the hash route.
#   shown      "" | "A" | "B": useLoad's page data (whose page it is).
#              Kept "" while away: a late answer there sets data the
#              unmounted view never shows, and the next Open clears it.
#   err        "" | "A" | "B": the read whose failure is on screen. Only
#              while nothing is shown: WikiPageView renders pageError only
#              when page is null, and setData(null) clears both together.
#   readA/B    a read of A / B is in flight. Two reads of one path
#              collapse into one (they answer with the same page).
#   editing    "" | "A" | "B": the editor is open with that page's body.
#   put        "" | "A>B" ...: the PUT in flight, body's page > path.
#              Save is disabled while one is (saving); a remount after
#              leaving the page would allow a second, which the model does
#              not take.
#   wrongwrite ghost: a PUT wrote one page's body to another's path.
#   late       ghost: a read answered on a screen whose key had changed,
#              and changed what it shows.

PAGES = ["A", "B"]

# WikiPageView's head: the shown page's path, else the route's.
def head(w):
    return w.shown if w.shown != "" else w.route

role Wiki:
    action Init:
        self.route = "away"
        self.shown = ""
        self.err = ""
        self.readA = False
        self.readB = False
        self.editing = ""
        self.put = ""
        self.wrongwrite = False
        self.late = False

    atomic func startRead(p):
        if p == "A":
            self.readA = True
        else:
            self.readB = True

    atomic func endRead(p):
        if p == "A":
            self.readA = False
        else:
            self.readB = False

    # setData / setErr with the view's reset effect after it: the editor
    # closes when the head moves.
    atomic func land(p, ok):
        self.endRead(p)
        if self.route == "away":
            return
        before = head(self)
        if ok:
            self.shown = p
            self.err = ""
        elif self.shown == "":
            self.err = p
        self.late = self.late or (p != self.route and (ok or self.shown == ""))
        if head(self) != before:
            self.editing = ""

    # A new page route: the key changes, data and error clear, a read of
    # the new path starts. The view stays mounted from page to page, so
    # the editor survives when the head does not move.
    atomic func open(p):
        before = head(self) if self.route != "away" else ""
        self.route = p
        self.shown = ""
        self.err = ""
        self.startRead(p)
        if head(self) != before:
            self.editing = ""

    # --- the person ----------------------------------------------------

    atomic action OpenA:
        require self.route != "A"
        self.open("A")

    atomic action OpenB:
        require self.route != "B"
        self.open("B")

    # To the index, Review or Activity: the page view unmounts.
    atomic action Away:
        require self.route != "away"
        self.route = "away"
        self.shown = ""
        self.err = ""
        self.editing = ""

    # The error's Retry: setErr(""), the current key's read again.
    atomic action Retry:
        require self.route != "away" and self.shown == "" and self.err != ""
        self.err = ""
        self.startRead(self.route)

    # Edit (header button or the menu): seeded from the page shown.
    atomic action Edit:
        require self.route != "away" and self.shown != "" and self.editing == ""
        self.editing = self.shown

    atomic action Cancel:
        require self.editing != "" and self.shown != ""
        self.editing = ""

    atomic action Save:
        require self.editing != "" and self.shown != "" and self.put == ""
        self.put = self.editing + ">" + self.route

    # --- the server ----------------------------------------------------

    atomic fair action AnswerA:
        require self.readA
        self.land("A", True)

    atomic fair action AnswerB:
        require self.readB
        self.land("B", True)

    atomic action FailA:
        require self.readA
        self.land("A", False)

    atomic action FailB:
        require self.readB
        self.land("B", False)

    # The PUT commits; the editor closes (setEditing(null) on whatever
    # page the view now shows, if it is mounted) and the saved path is
    # read again with the load of the render Save was clicked in.
    atomic fair action SaveOk:
        require self.put != ""
        body = self.put[0]
        path = self.put[2]
        self.wrongwrite = self.wrongwrite or body != path
        self.put = ""
        self.editing = ""
        self.startRead(path)

    # The editor stays open with its text and the error above it.
    atomic action SaveFail:
        require self.put != ""
        self.put = ""

action Init:
    wiki = Wiki()

# The editor holds the body of the page at the view's head: the reset
# effect closes it whenever the shown page changes.
always assertion EditorHoldsHeadPage:
    return wiki.editing == "" or (wiki.route != "away" and wiki.editing == head(wiki))

# A PUT carries the text of a page the editor was opened on, to the route
# it was clicked on.
always assertion PutIsEditorToRoute:
    return wiki.put == "" or (wiki.put[0] in PAGES and wiki.put[2] in PAGES)

# A failure is on screen only over nothing shown.
always assertion ErrorOnlyOverNothing:
    return wiki.err == "" or (wiki.shown == "" and wiki.route != "away")

# A page route does not stay loading: it shows a page or an error.
always eventually assertion PageRouteSettles:
    return wiki.route == "away" or wiki.shown != "" or wiki.err != ""

# Saving always ends.
always eventually assertion SavingEnds:
    return wiki.put == ""

# No "every read ends" claim: a person who keeps reopening a page keeps a
# read of it in flight, and fizz rightly finds that fair cycle. Each read
# answering is what AnswerA/AnswerB's fairness says.
